    {
      "block_id": "h2-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "`build_receipt()` Behavior",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Accepts `WriteFileResult` → returns `WriteFileReceipt` - Explicitly excludes `content` field from receipt - Uses `result.after_bytes` directly (file stat after write) - Uses `result.before_bytes` directly (snapshot content length) - Uses `result.duration_ms` directly (wall-clock timing from run()) - Sanitizes `refusal_reason` via `_sanitize_refusal_for_receipt()` (currently pass-through, guard does not embed content)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-11",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Remaining Gaps",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. **ToolError bypass paths** — **COMPLETED**: Directory, size, exists, and missing-parent errors now yield structured `WriteFileResult(status=\"refused\")` results instead of raising `ToolError`. See `docs/audits/tool-hardening/write-file-legacy-result-content-audit.md` for the full audit. 2. **`content` still in WriteFileResult** — Legacy callers may depend on it. Safe to remove only after auditing all callers. 3. **`before_sha256` only for success path** — Blocked/refused paths set it to None. This is correct behavior since the guard/snapshot runs before write. 4. **Permission preservation** — Only mode bits (via chmod) are preserved after atomic replace. ACLs/xattrs are dropped.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Schema Validation",
