      "content": "Atomic Write Implementation",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "WriteFile now uses an atomic temp-file + replace pattern instead of direct write:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `_atomic_write_text()` static method on `WriteFile` class - Uses `tempfile.mkstemp()` for same-directory temp file (ensuring cross-device safety) - Writes content via `os.write()`, then `os.fsync()` before close - Preserves existing file mode via `chmod()` if overwriting - Atomic replace via `os.replace()` (POSIX atomic rename semantics) - Best-effort parent directory `os.fsync()` for durable persistence - On failure: cleans up temp file and re-raises - Called from `_write_file()` via `asyncio.to_thread()` for async compatibility - Bounded by `max_write_bytes` (64 KB), so synchronous I/O is acceptable",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
